From 21c4270ac746c75c6366dbdc3ff6eebdf83e421b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:40:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] hub admission: judge pre-gate hub-local cards at
 claim time

The hub dispatcher claimed its own pre-gate cards (runs_on and placement_policy
NULL, no hub_admission verdict) on hub slots unjudged: admission runs at create,
move, courier landing and foreign pickup, and the claim backstop
(pickup.refusals) only covers foreign hub-bound copies. On 11-12 the hourly pin
sweep moved 7 such cards off the hub by hand after their runs; 26 more waited.

Before the claim pass, the hub now judges each ready, label-less card with no
verdict (kanban_hub_admission_claim.screen, from the worker_pickup seam,
outside any write txn) and records a hub_admission event with entry=claim:
- admit: claimed as before;
- deny: re-placed with the pickup deny route (worker-queue labels, +hub-write
  when portable_reason hits; never machine:worker-N), moved event citing the
  verdict, not claimed;
- deny that must stay (structural_reason, requires host_repo, a hub worktree
  path in the brief, a hub-local wake_check, no worker queue fits): kept=<why>,
  claimed as before;
- judge unavailable: claimed as before (fail open), no verdict, judged at the
  next ready; one outage per tick skips the rest.
Any existing verdict (forced/skipped too) makes no model call. Each acting tick
logs 'hub admission: claim screen judged=N denied=N moved=N kept=N
unavailable=N', and hermes doctor on the hub counts its claims of unjudged
cards in the last 7 days (should be 0).

Task: t_01a1d09606b75027
